// @run
// @log true
// @log true
// @log 7
// CONTRACT (must-RUN): D902. A `??` joins two same-fieldset object literals whose leaf atoms
// are `boolean` and `null`. D804's mint builds the merged row but DECLINED field code 21, so
// the field fell back to `anonFieldCode`'s plain boolean, `emitObj`'s code-21 leg never seeded
// `pendingNulBool`, and the `{ r: null }` operand reached `emitNullLitNode` with none of its
// seven seeds set: `emitProgram: bare null needs a struct-typed context`, `vl check` rc 0.
//
// THE CLOSE IS THE NICHE AND NOT A BOX. The field is `(struct (field (mut i32)))` holding 0/1
// for the booleans and the sentinel 2 for `null` — no `{tag, payload}` struct is emitted for
// this pair at all.
//
// IT WAS NEVER A MINT-ONLY GAP. `declared` below declares `type R = { r: boolean | null }` and
// still took the loud reject on master, as did the annotated-binding and parameter-typed
// spellings. What ran on master is the `??` default given its own declared binding — the
// literal in DEFAULT position is the whole of it.
//
// AND THE MAP TRADE D804 DECLINED THE RUNG OVER IS PAID. D804's header states that an `#anon`
// row carrying code 21 interns no map-value slot, so the pair would swap `bare null needs a
// struct-typed context` for `unsupported map value type`. That is exactly what admitting 21
// alone does. The mv gap is ONE line: `structIndexOfTypeName`'s third pass is handed the
// field's TEXT, so the boolean/i32 distinction code 0 erased is recoverable there —
// `fieldCodeWidensElem`'s twin is handed two CODES, cannot make it, and still refuses. With
// both rungs `mapjoin` below RUNS.
//
// NOT IN THIS FILE, and it is a different row: a callee that returns a BARE `null`
// (`function s(): {n: boolean} | null { null }` beside `?? { n: null }`) contributes no
// literal at all, so the set is one atom, no row is minted and the reject stands. That is
// D893's shape — the callee's own return annotation is the atom nobody reads — filed OPEN,
// and it refuses identically on master.

function src(): {r: boolean} | null { { r: true } }
function rd() {
  const g1 = src() ?? { r: null }
  print(g1.r)
}
rd()

type R = { q: boolean | null }
function declSrc(): R | null { { q: true } }
function declared() {
  const g3 = declSrc() ?? { q: null }
  print(g3.q)
}
declared()

function mapjoin() {
  const c = Map()
  c["k0"] = { m: true }
  const g4 = (c)["k0"] ?? { m: null }
  if (g4).m != null { print(7) } else { print(0) }
}
mapjoin()
